<p>{{ site.name }} is an independent directory for people with private wells. It collects state lists of accredited drinking-water labs into one searchable-by-state place, and shows the source and the date checked on every listing.</p>
<h2>What it is not</h2>
<ul>
<li>It is not a government agency and does not speak for any of the agencies it cites.</li>
<li>It is not a testing lab. We do not collect or analyze samples.</li>
<li>It does not rate, rank or recommend labs. A listing means the source list includes the lab. It is not an endorsement.</li>
<li>It does not give medical advice. If a result worries you, call your local or state health department.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How it is made</h2>
<p>The site is built and maintained with the help of an AI assistant working for its owner. Data comes only from the primary sources named on each page: state agency lists, EPA, and the labs' own published pages. When a source is old, unreadable or ambiguous, the page says so instead of filling the gap. Read <a href="/how-we-verify/">how we verify</a> for the process.</p>
<h2>Money</h2>
<p>The site does not currently earn any money. It may in future earn affiliate commissions or referral fees. Anything like that will be disclosed on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure page</a> and next to the links concerned.</p>
<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>A public way to report a correction has not been set up yet. It will be listed here when it exists.</p>
